infographic list-column-simple-vertical-arrow
data
  title The three taxes of an oversized pool
  desc Every connection past the hardware ceiling drags on all the others
  lists
    - label Context switching
      desc OS time-slices 100 connections across 8 cores; each switch flushes CPU caches and burns scheduler time — the box spends CPU choosing which query runs, not running queries.
    - label Lock & latch contention
      desc Shared internal latches — buffer pool, WAL, lock tables — contend super-linearly, so it worsens faster than the connection count grows.
    - label Per-connection memory
      desc ~2–3 MB baseline per Postgres backend, plus work_mem (16 MB) allocated per operation per connection — a sort across 100 connections can reserve gigabytes.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b #f43f5e
